From e3819b3173150bbdc3ebff525515bb162837d2cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): preserve workspace handoffs in role-specific guidance

The generic Kanban patch assigns separate contracts to workers and live
orchestrators.  Keep this deployment's workspace-output choreography out of
that backend-independent patch while retaining the producer-owned child and
trusted revision handoff required by the Gondolin workspace broker.

Compact the worker contract around terminal-state and publication invariants.
Only workspace-revision inheritance requires the live orchestrator to create
the producer alone; ordinary parent dependencies and summary/metadata handoffs
continue to use normal pre-created task graphs.
---
